# Cached integer tables for the literal J₂ Schreier edges

The seven long integers concatenate the unchanged 128-entry packed blocks.
Four more concatenate the already certified transversal maps, and two cache
subgroup-power maps and generator images of the four base points. Their exact
comparison with the original definitions is proved in `Edges.Checker`.
No equality or edge assertion is inferred from the transcription.

Source: Geometry/source/README.md, Coordinates/source/README.md and the ATLAS
attribution in Presentation/source/README.md. Reproduction: Edges/source/generate.py.
-/

